WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.697
Most computer-use agents live inside a browser, or a VM,

00:00:04.697 --> 00:00:08.189
or they grab your mouse like a clumsy intern.

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:09.509
aos is different.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:11.837
It's a CLI and an agent skill.

00:00:11.837 --> 00:00:18.124
Install it once, and your agent can arrange your windows, open apps, click, type,

00:00:18.124 --> 00:00:21.850
show you where to click, and record what it did.

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:26.065
Let's start where every desk gets messy:

00:00:26.065 --> 00:00:26.661
windows.

00:00:26.661 --> 00:00:30.761
One short command puts an app exactly where it belongs.

00:00:30.761 --> 00:00:35.233
A half, a quarter, a third, on whichever monitor you choose.

00:00:36.483 --> 00:00:38.306
Need a page, or an app?

00:00:38.306 --> 00:00:43.138
aos opens it, waits for the window, and puts it in its place.

00:00:43.138 --> 00:00:47.733
The same command works on a Mac, on Windows, and on Linux.

00:00:48.983 --> 00:00:51.885
Now the part pixel-guessers can't do.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:58.551
aos finds a button by its name, straight from the accessibility tree, and presses it.

00:00:58.551 --> 00:01:02.316
No screenshots, no coordinates, no vision model.

00:01:02.316 --> 00:01:03.649
Seven, times six.

00:01:03.649 --> 00:01:04.433
Forty-two.

00:01:05.683 --> 00:01:07.837
And it never steals your keyboard.

00:01:07.837 --> 00:01:13.286
Text goes straight to the app you name, even while you keep working in another window.

00:01:13.286 --> 00:01:16.833
Then verify reads it back, so the agent knows it landed.

00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:21.222
Sometimes you'd rather do it yourself.

00:01:21.222 --> 00:01:22.627
So aos shows you.

00:01:22.627 --> 00:01:28.244
It draws an arrow, a label, or a subtitle right on your real screen,

00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:31.383
and your clicks pass straight through.

00:01:32.617 --> 00:01:35.755
Now hand it to an agent, in plain English.

00:01:35.755 --> 00:01:41.433
The skill teaches Claude Code every command, so one sentence becomes a plan:

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:45.767
launch, arrange, type, check, and point you at the result.

00:01:47.017 --> 00:01:49.767
Here's the same thing on Windows.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:53.017
Same binary, same commands, same skill.

00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:57.694
And when the work is done, aos can record it.

00:01:57.694 --> 00:02:04.137
Start a smart capture, stop it, and the camera has already zoomed in on every action.

00:02:04.137 --> 00:02:08.533
Every clip you just watched was recorded exactly that way.

00:02:09.783 --> 00:02:11.589
Install it with one line.

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:16.139
install dot S H on Mac and Linux, install dot C M D on Windows.

00:02:16.139 --> 00:02:21.194
The skill installs itself, so your agent is ready the moment it lands.

00:02:21.194 --> 00:02:21.483
aos.

00:02:21.483 --> 00:02:25.383
Let your AI use your computer, without taking it over.
